:"2017-08-17T23:04:07Z","updated_at":"2017-08-20T19:34:31Z","body":"I have also encountered exactly the same problem. Here is a test code.\r\n```test.py\r\nfrom __future__ import print_function\r\n\r\nimport sklearn\r\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import SparseCoder\r\nfrom sklearn.svm import LinearSVC\r\nfrom sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\r\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import GridSearchCV\r\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import Normalizer\r\nfrom sklearn.datasets import load_iris\r\n\r\nimport numpy as np\r\n\r\n# versions\r\nprint('scikit-learn ', sklearn.__version__)\r\nprint('numpy ', np.__version__)\r\n\r\n# parameters\r\nn_samples_dict = 5\r\n\r\n# training samples\r\niris = load_iris()\r\n# Take the first two features. We could avoid this by using a two-dim dataset\r\nX_train = iris.data\r\ny_train = iris.target\r\n\r\n# dictionary\r\nrand_dict = Normalizer(norm='l2').transform(X_train[:n_samples_dict])\r\n\r\n# models\r\nsp = SparseCoder(dictionary=rand_dict, transform_algorithm='threshold')\r\nsvm = LinearSVC()\r\npipeline = Pipeline([ ('sp', sp), ('svm', svm) ])\r\n\r\n# grid search\r\ngrid = {'sp__transform_alpha': [0.1, 1, 10], 'svm__C': [0.1, 1, 10]}\r\nmodel = GridSearchCV(estimator=pipeline, param_grid=grid, scoring='accuracy')\r\n\r\n# check\r\nprint('Components: \\n', model.estimator.named_steps['sp'].components_)\r\nprint('Sparse coder: \\n', model.estimator.named_steps['sp'])\r\nprint('Sparse coder: \\n', sp)\r\nprint('Sparse coder: \\n', SparseCoder(dictionary=rand_dict.copy(), transform_algorithm='threshold'))\r\n\r\n# test\r\nX_transformed = sp.transform(X_train)\r\nprint('original: \\n', X_train[5:10])\r\nprint('transformed: \\n', X_transformed[5:10])\r\n\r\n# fit\r\nmodel.fit(X_train, y_train)\r\nprint(model.best_estimator_)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe result is the following. \"Components_\" in the sparse coder looks like correct, but the sparse coder instance itself seems to fail the initialisation.\r\n\r\n```\r\n# python test.py\r\nscikit-learn  0.19.0\r\nnumpy  1.13.0\r\nComponents: \r\n [[ 0.80377277  0.55160877  0.22064351  0.0315205 ]\r\n [ 0.82813287  0.50702013  0.23660939  0.03380134]\r\n [ 0.80533308  0.54831188  0.2227517   0.03426949]\r\n [ 0.80003025  0.53915082  0.26087943  0.03478392]\r\n [ 0.790965    0.5694948   0.2214702   0.0316386 ]]\r\nSparse coder: \r\n SparseCoder(dictionary=None, n_jobs=1, split_sign=False,\r\n      transform_algorithm='threshold', transform_alpha=None,\r\n      transform_n_nonzero_coefs=None)\r\nSparse coder: \r\n SparseCoder(dictionary=None, n_jobs=1, split_sign=False,\r\n      transform_algorithm='threshold', transform_alpha=None,\r\n      transform_n_nonzero_coefs=None)\r\nSparse coder: \r\n SparseCoder(dictionary=None, n_jobs=1, split_sign=False,\r\n      transform_algorithm='threshold', transform_alpha=None,\r\n      transform_n_nonzero_coefs=None)\r\noriginal: \r\n [[ 5.4  3.9  1.7  0.4]\r\n [ 4.6  3.4  1.4  0.3]\r\n [ 5.   3.4  1.5  0.2]\r\n [ 4.4  2.9  1.4  0.2]\r\n [ 4.9  3.1  1.5  0.1]]\r\ntransformed: \r\n [[ 5.87934932  5.86505251  5.87960063  5.88026013  5.88139547]\r\n [ 4.89118162  4.8746732   4.89092577  4.8889183   4.89427115]\r\n [ 5.23160303  5.22620715  5.23190722  5.23153995  5.22964031]\r\n [ 4.45147063  4.45215643  4.45227627  4.45585845  4.4481669 ]\r\n [ 4.98259107  4.98790769  4.9834534   4.98631329  4.97653151]]\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"sparse_coder_test.py\", line 54, in <module>\r\n    model.fit(X_train, y_train)\r\n  File \"/Users/akisato/.pyenv/versions/anaconda-4.0.0/lib/python2.7/site-packages/sklearn/model_selection/_search.py\", line 624, in fit\r\n    base_estimator = clone(self.estimator)\r\n  File \"/Users/akisato/.pyenv/versions/anaconda-4.0.0/lib/python2.7/site-packages/sklearn/base.py\", line 61, in clone\r\n    new_object_params[name] = clone(param, safe=False)\r\n  File \"/Users/akisato/.pyenv/versions/anaconda-4.0.0/lib/python2.7/site-packages/sklearn/base.py\", line 49, in clone\r\n    return estimator_type([clone(e, safe=safe) for e in estimator])\r\n  File \"/Users/akisato/.pyenv/versions/anaconda-4.0.0/lib/python2.7/site-packages/sklearn/base.py\", line 49, in clone\r\n    return estimator_type([clone(e, safe=safe) for e in estimator])\r\n  File \"/Users/akisato/.pyenv/versions/anaconda-4.0.0/lib/python2.7/site-packages/sklearn/base.py\", line 62, in clone\r\n    new_object = klass(**new_object_params)\r\n  File \"/Users/akisato/.pyenv/versions/anaconda-4.0.0/lib/python2.7/site-packages/sklearn/decomposition/dict_learning.py\", line 916, in __init__\r\n    self._set_sparse_coding_params(dictionary.shape[0],\r\nAttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'shape'\r\n```\r\n\r\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scikit-learn/scikit-learn/issues/comments/323217280/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"akisatok","id":7335205,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczMzUyMDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7335205?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akisatok","html_url":"https://github.com/akisatok","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akisatok/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akisatok/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akisatok/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akisatok/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akisatok/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akisatok/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akisatok/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akisatok/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akisatok/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scikit-learn/scikit-learn/